evidence[2]{path,hash,excerpt,truncated}:
  ".project/done-work.md#agent-model-sweep","sha256:d207492b68efd942019db2dc0b051928817336a5ff12b5d907ed157873147938","## agent-model-sweep — shipped 2026-10-16\n\nTwo bets on one pitch (bundle 2.28.0, 2026-10-16). Bet 1 made `workflow-doctor.mts` read the toon `models` block, added a top-level `checkToonMandatory()` and had `extractAgentProfile` read a `profile:` frontmatter key. Bet 2 (the canonical sweep): 16 `.claude/agents/*.md` gained `profile: fast|standard|deep` and lost `model:`; the 16 Cursor mirrors were regenerated byte-identical in the same commit (no drift window); `.opencode/opencode.json` got a top-level `model:` equal to `models.opencode.deep.model` and lost `agent.build.model`, which preserves the deep primary-agent routing; the legacy `claude-haiku-/sonnet-/opus-` model-prefix fallback in the doctor was deleted (a canonical agent without `profile:` warns, per the pinned decision's \"when to revisit\"); a new `agent-frontmatter-invariant.test.mts` pins presence, allowlist, no `model:` and valid YAML; docs (`extending.md`, `vendors.md`, `harnesses.md`) say Claude Code does not read the toon and the profile is declared once; `CHANGELOG` 2.28.0. Commits `9a336a2` (Bet 2) and `7c7643c` (audit patches).\n\nNo-gos held: no agent prompt-body changes (`profile:` is frontmatter), no dependencies or network, no secrets, no TOON grammar or `config.mts` changes, no aliases or fallback chains. `model:` in `.opencode/agents/*.md`, `.codex/agents/*.toml` and `.opencode/commands/*.md` stays for Bet 3. Rabbit holes: the doctor derives the profile from frontmatter, not a body banner or the model id; mirror consistency anchors on the line, not a substring; exception tables and project-owned routing (`modelRouting: project`) were preserved; per-role overrides, generating vendor config from the toon and runtime model switching were pushed to no-go; whether Claude Code runs without `model:` frontmatter was the named Bet 2 precondition and held.\n\nDeviations: S1 and S2 shipped as one commit because the byte-identity test fails if the canonical edit ships alone; the opencode.json shell exit chec",true
  ".project/knowledge/patterns/warn-text-must-be-self-consistent-with-the-code-it-ships.md","sha256:96a72f9818e1b9c1ca136154c75c1efe60dc162f64bd8f56caf420940f6676d2","---\nid: warn-text-must-be-self-consistent-with-the-code-it-ships\ntype: pattern\ncreated: 2026-10-16\nupdated: 2026-10-16\ntags: [validation, doctor, error-messages, consistency]\nrelated: [a-gate-must-not-trust-its-own-author, mandatory-config-files-emit-one-top-level-failure]\nsource: agent-model-sweep\n---\n\n# Pattern: Warn text must be self-consistent with the code it ships\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen a code path is removed or its behavior changes, every `record(...)` / `throw` / `console.warn`\nmessage that referenced the old path must be updated in the same commit. Operators who read\nthe message will look for behavior that no longer exists; the message contradicts the code.\n\n## What happened\n\n`agent-model-sweep` Bet 2 removed the legacy `claude-haiku-` / `sonnet-` / `opus-` model-prefix\nfallback in `workflow-doctor.mts`'s `extractAgentProfile` (per the pinned decision\n`profile-detection-lives-in-frontmatter-not-in-the-model-id` \"When to Revisit\" clause). The\n`checkAgent` warn at `workflow-doctor.mts:800` was not updated; it still said:\n\n> no declared capability profile — add a `profile: fast|standard|deep` frontmatter key, **or a\n> `model:` line whose prefix matches a known claude-haiku-/sonnet-/opus- tier (legacy\n> fallback)**\n\nThe operator who reads this message tries to add the `model:` line and expects the doctor\nto derive a profile. It does not — the fallback is gone, the `model:` line is ignored, and\nthe same warn fires forever. The code-reviewer flagged this in audit cycle 1 as a must-fix;\nthe security-reviewer flagged the same item as \"documentation accuracy.\"\n\n## The fix\n\nWhen removing or changing a code path, grep for every user-facing message that mentions\nthe path. Update the messages in the same commit. Add a test that asserts the new wording\n(see `warn-text-patches-need-their-own-test-assertion`).\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Removing a feature, branch, or fallback in any file that emits operator-facing messages\n  (`record(...)`, `throw new Error(...)`, `console.warn`, `cons",true
